  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 228 PM MDT TUE SEP 15 2026\nThe upper-level low pressure system will continue to move through \nthe area Friday into early Saturday. Precipitation / thunderstorm \nchances and overall coverage will be lower compared to Thursday, \nwith the primary threat area being the west-central Idaho mountains \nand Baker County. Chances will range from at least a 30-70% chance \nof showers and a 10-25% chance of thunderstorms through Friday \nnight. Over the weekend starting Saturday afternoon, upper-level \nridging builds in causing warming and drying conditions. \nTemperatures will start slightly below normal and trend slightly \nabove normal (3-5 degrees) by Monday. An upper-level troughing \npattern looks to return by early-to-mid next week, bringing slightly \ncooler temperatures and a slight chance of mountain rain\nshowers.",
